1
00:00:00,899 --> 00:00:09,560
Welcome to South Africa's provinces, part 1 of 1. First, I clear the chosen
names for a fresh regional lesson.

2
00:00:10,221 --> 00:00:20,159
We work through 9 of the South Africa regions the map names, once each: where
it sits, one fact worth keeping, and a hook to remember it by.

3
00:00:20,828 --> 00:00:23,127
Let's bring Limpopo into view.

4
00:00:29,392 --> 00:00:40,096
Limpopo lies in the far north-east of South Africa, inland, next to Gauteng,
Mpumalanga and the North West, with Thohoyandou as its largest town.

5
00:00:40,754 --> 00:00:49,798
Mapungubwe was the centre of a kingdom here in the thirteenth century, and
archaeologists found a small golden rhinoceros in one of its royal graves.

6
00:00:50,464 --> 00:00:58,730
Remember the province named for the Limpopo river in the far north-east, with
a golden rhinoceros buried in its mountain kingdom.

7
00:00:59,419 --> 00:01:02,310
Let's bring Mpumalanga into view.

8
00:01:07,282 --> 00:01:18,579
Mpumalanga lies in the north-east of the interior, landlocked between Limpopo,
Gauteng, the Free State and KwaZulu-Natal, with Mbombela as its largest city.

9
00:01:19,229 --> 00:01:28,529
Its name means the place where the sun rises, and the southern half of the
Kruger National Park, opened in 1926, lies inside it.

10
00:01:29,193 --> 00:01:37,982
Remember the rising sun in the east, with half of the Kruger and some of the
oldest rocks on earth around Barberton.

11
00:01:38,663 --> 00:01:41,391
Let's bring Gauteng into view.

12
00:01:46,089 --> 00:01:59,696
Gauteng is the smallest province by area but the most crowded, in the
north-east of the interior, with Johannesburg as its largest city and
Pretoria, the administrative capital, beside it.

13
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:17,064
Its Sesotho name means place of gold, for the gold reef on the Witwatersrand,
and the Cradle of Humankind lies here, where the Sterkfontein caves gave up
Mrs Ples, a fossil about two and a half million years old.

14
00:02:17,728 --> 00:02:25,356
Remember the crowded little province of gold, with some of the oldest human
ancestor fossils in its caves.

15
00:02:26,065 --> 00:02:28,828
Let's bring North West into view.

16
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:48,085
The North West lies in the centre of the country, inland, next to the Free
State, Gauteng, Limpopo and the Northern Cape, with Klerksdorp as its largest
town.

17
00:02:48,746 --> 00:03:02,945
Much of it was once Bophuthatswana, a homeland declared independent under
apartheid that no other country recognised, and the Pilanesberg reserve lies
inside the ring of an ancient extinct volcano.

18
00:03:03,608 --> 00:03:08,682
Remember the north-western province with a game reserve ringed by an ancient
volcano.

19
00:03:09,425 --> 00:03:12,060
Let's bring Free State into view.

20
00:03:18,513 --> 00:03:30,367
The Free State sits in the middle of South Africa, landlocked, touching six
other provinces including the Northern Cape and the Eastern Cape, with
Bloemfontein as its largest city.

21
00:03:31,025 --> 00:03:45,270
Its name comes from the Orange Free State, the Boer republic of 1854 to 1902,
and the Vredefort crater inside it is about two billion years old, the largest
impact structure known on earth.

22
00:03:45,922 --> 00:03:53,643
Remember the flat central province of the old Boer republic, with the biggest
meteorite scar on the planet inside it.

23
00:03:54,482 --> 00:03:56,734
Let's bring Northern Cape into view.

24
00:04:05,479 --> 00:04:14,941
The Northern Cape is the biggest province in the country and the one with the
fewest people, filling the north-west and reaching the Atlantic coast, with
Kimberley as its largest town.

25
00:04:15,594 --> 00:04:26,298
After the winter rains the semi-desert of Namaqualand is covered in wild
flowers, and the town of Kimberley grew rich on the diamonds dug from the mine
beneath it.

26
00:04:26,951 --> 00:04:34,323
Remember the huge, thinly peopled province in the west, a land of diamonds and
spring flowers.

27
00:04:35,053 --> 00:04:37,944
Let's bring KwaZulu-Natal into view.

28
00:04:44,005 --> 00:04:56,463
KwaZulu-Natal runs down the east coast on the Indian Ocean, with Durban as its
largest city, and it touches the Eastern Cape, the Free State and Mpumalanga
inland.

29
00:04:57,121 --> 00:05:11,924
Natal is the name Vasco da Gama gave this coast when he sailed past it on
Christmas Day in 1497, and the Drakensberg mountains along its western edge
hold thousands of San rock paintings in a UNESCO park.

30
00:05:12,582 --> 00:05:19,745
Remember the Zulu coast on the Indian Ocean, with the high wall of the
Drakensberg rising behind it.

31
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:22,712
Let's bring Eastern Cape into view.

32
00:05:29,707 --> 00:05:45,043
The Eastern Cape curves round the south-east of the country along the Indian
Ocean, with Gqeberha as its largest city, and it borders the Northern Cape,
the Free State, KwaZulu-Natal and the Western Cape.

33
00:05:45,703 --> 00:05:59,647
Nelson Mandela was born in the small village of Mvezo here in 1918, and from
1779 the Xhosa people fought nine frontier wars against the colonists over
about a century.

34
00:06:00,305 --> 00:06:07,805
Remember the south-eastern coast where Mandela was born and the Xhosa fought
nine wars for their land.

35
00:06:08,503 --> 00:06:11,011
Let's bring Western Cape into view.

36
00:06:16,593 --> 00:06:29,724
The Western Cape fills the south-west corner of the country, where the
Atlantic coast meets False Bay, with Cape Town as its largest city, and it
borders the Northern Cape and the Eastern Cape.

37
00:06:30,382 --> 00:06:46,258
The province is named for the Cape of Good Hope, which Bartolomeu Dias rounded
in 1488 and the king of Portugal so called. Its fynbos is the heart of the
Cape Floral Kingdom, the smallest of the world’s six plant kingdoms.

38
00:06:46,913 --> 00:06:53,217
Remember the Cape of Good Hope at the south-west tip, with its own tiny
kingdom of plants.

39
00:06:59,003 --> 00:07:15,203
9 regions of South Africa, one for each target of the map: Limpopo,
Mpumalanga, Gauteng, North West, Free State, Northern Cape, KwaZulu-Natal,
Eastern Cape and Western Cape.

40
00:07:15,862 --> 00:07:27,077
Remember the shape of South Africa from the inside: the regions nest around
each other, and every name on the map belongs somewhere in this one country.
